From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Map diagnostic code RX and mutable state RW-NX before the TTBR1 switch

Diagnostic hook, a no-op unless both diagnostic segments are present.

The early-reporter appends __KDIAG code and __KDATRW state/stack segments past
__BOOTDATA, in the gap between __BOOTDATA and dynamic_memory_begin.
arm_vm_prot_init() does not otherwise map this gap. Both parts must be mapped
before the TTBR1 switch: code is RX, while the reporter state and private stack
are RW-NX. Mapping only the code would fault as soon as the reporter stores state.

The lookup is unconditional and uses names rather than boot arguments. Both
segments must be present, contiguous and 16 KiB aligned; otherwise neither is
mapped. A kernel without the diagnostic pair therefore behaves as before.

Not a functional fix. This keeps a no-console early reporter reachable across
the TTBR1 switch.
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -1801,7 +1801,24 @@ arm_vm_prot_init(__unused boot_args * args)
 	if (segLASTDATACONSTB) {
 		arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segLASTDATACONSTB, segSizeLASTDATACONST, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK); // __LASTDATA_CONST may be empty, but we cannot assume this
 	}
 	arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segPRELINKDATAB, segSizePRELINKDATA, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK | ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT); // Prelink __DATA for kexts (RW data)
+
+	/* TB710FU diagnostics: map appended code RX and state RW-NX. */
+	{
+		unsigned long diag_rx_size = 0, diag_rw_size = 0;
+		vm_offset_t diag_rx_base = (vm_offset_t)getsegdatafromheader(
+		    &_mh_execute_header, "__KDIAG", &diag_rx_size);
+		vm_offset_t diag_rw_base = (vm_offset_t)getsegdatafromheader(
+		    &_mh_execute_header, "__KDATRW", &diag_rw_size);
+		if (diag_rx_base && diag_rx_size && diag_rw_base && diag_rw_size &&
+		    diag_rw_base > diag_rx_base &&
+		    diag_rw_base - diag_rx_base == diag_rx_size &&
+		    ((diag_rx_base | diag_rx_size | diag_rw_base | diag_rw_size) & 0x3fff) == 0) {
+			arm_vm_page_granular_ROX(diag_rx_base, diag_rx_size, 0,
+			    ARM64_PAGE_UNGUARDED);
+			arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(diag_rw_base, diag_rw_size, 0);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (segSizePLKLLVMCOV > 0) {
 		arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segPLKLLVMCOVB, segSizePLKLLVMCOV, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK | ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT); // LLVM code coverage data
